<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vilmos Tkálecz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1894–1950</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vilmos Tkálecz was a Slovene-speaking teacher and politician from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prekmurje">Prekmurje</a> region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>. On 29 May 1919, during the turmoil of the Hungarian Soviet Republic, he proclaimed the independent Republic of Prekmurje, or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mur-river">Mura</a> Republic, at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murska-sobota">Murska Sobota</a>; it was crushed within days, and the region passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a> that August.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vilmos-tkalecz.jpg" alt="Vilmos Tkálecz" width="320" height="459" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tk%C3%A1lecz_Vilmos_%C3%A9s_feles%C3%A9ge.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
